1
00:00:59,320 --> 00:01:00,240
Don't be nervous.

2
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:01,080
I mean no harm.

3
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:03,120
I just want to know the truth.

4
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:05,970
Then find out yourself.

5
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,520
What are you doing?

6
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:09,320
We need to get going.

7
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:15,039
The road to Dabei Temple is too long.

8
00:01:15,039 --> 00:01:16,560
I'm exhausted.

9
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:17,800
I rode it.

10
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:20,650
I told you we wouldn't find him.

11
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:23,920
He probably starved to death during the famine.

12
00:01:24,120 --> 00:01:25,440
Someone wants us to solve the case.

13
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:26,600
And someone doesn't.

14
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:28,120
This mysterious person is something else.

15
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:29,960
Giving clues is like pulling teeth.

16
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:32,090
They won't tell us anything straight.

17
00:01:32,440 --> 00:01:34,170
We're in the middle of nowhere.

18
00:01:34,320 --> 00:01:35,320
Let's look ahead.

19
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:36,520
Let's go.

20
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:37,840
I'm starving.

21
00:01:39,039 --> 00:01:39,840
Boss.

22
00:01:39,960 --> 00:01:41,320
What are they trying to do?

23
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:43,180
Aren't they just messing with us?

24
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:44,840
Cut the crap.

25
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,000
Just follow them.

26
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:47,920
It's just simple peasant food.

27
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:48,720
Please enjoy your meal.

28
00:01:48,720 --> 00:01:49,650
Thank you, miss.

29
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:50,880
Smells great.

30
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:52,080
This is such a feast.

31
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:56,960
You mean the two of them are...

32
00:01:58,720 --> 00:01:59,520
What's wrong?

33
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,130
Look at that flower.

34
00:02:10,039 --> 00:02:11,700
My investigation led me here.

35
00:02:12,120 --> 00:02:12,600
Look.

36
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:15,140
The soil on this grave is freshly turned.

37
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,200
It's this smell.

38
00:02:19,360 --> 00:02:19,880
Sister.

39
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:21,640
This steamed bun tastes very special.

40
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:22,600
What is it made of?

41
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:23,920
You might not know this.

42
00:02:23,920 --> 00:02:25,200
This is a poor place.

43
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:26,120
During the famine,

44
00:02:26,120 --> 00:02:27,720
we couldn't even afford steamed buns.

45
00:02:27,720 --> 00:02:29,520
So I added some elm seeds to it.

46
00:02:29,520 --> 00:02:31,720
This way, it tastes good and fills you up.

47
00:02:31,720 --> 00:02:33,560
The taste is quite special.

48
00:02:34,040 --> 00:02:34,640
Miss.

49
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:35,520
Where is your husband?

50
00:02:35,520 --> 00:02:36,960
He's a good-for-nothing.

51
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:38,280
He's eating inside by himself.

52
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:39,210
Enjoy your meal.

53
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:55,320
Zhao Bin.

54
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:03,440
You are Zhao Bin.

55
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:05,320
What are you talking about?

56
00:03:05,320 --> 00:03:06,450
I don't understand.

57
00:03:08,320 --> 00:03:09,400
A few days ago, we went

58
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,240
to pay our respects at Wei Xiaodong's grave.

59
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:13,520
There were the same yellow irises

60
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:15,900
and the same special steamed cornbread.

61
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:18,360
You have the wrong person.

62
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:19,280
We know

63
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:21,720
you were the one who went to pay respects to Wei Xiaodong.

64
00:03:21,720 --> 00:03:22,640
Since

65
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:24,520
you were willing to visit Wei Xiaodong,

66
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:25,600
it means you don't want him

67
00:03:25,600 --> 00:03:27,040
to die an unexplained death.

68
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:28,320
If you think of anything,

69
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:30,720
come find us at the police station anytime.

70
00:03:31,079 --> 00:03:31,960
Let's go.

71
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:39,520
Thank you, sir.

72
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:40,800
Still, thank you for your hospitality today.

73
00:03:40,800 --> 00:03:41,730
Brother Shi'an,

74
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:44,040
I sincerely want to be friends with you.

75
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:45,720
Don't treat me so coldly.

76
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:48,520
If you really wanted to be friends,

77
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:50,120
you wouldn't have doubted her.

78
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:51,640
If you dare to mess around,

79
00:03:52,120 --> 00:03:54,120
don't blame me for not holding back.

80
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:55,320
I didn't.

81
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:56,720
I, Zhou Wei, swear

82
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,960
I just admire Inspector Jiang

83
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:01,040
and appreciate Brother Shi'an.

84
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,400
Huo Yining is also quite good.

85
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:06,200
Really.

86
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:07,520
I just admire you

87
00:04:07,720 --> 00:04:10,580
and want to compare notes on solving cases with you.

88
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:28,080
Let's go.

89
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,760
Can you ride a bit faster?

90
00:04:46,159 --> 00:04:47,520
I want to go faster too.

91
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:51,520
Why is this little bandit riding so fast?

92
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:54,100
Should we help him?

93
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:54,970
Help.

94
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:56,400
Help who?

95
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:57,640
Help both of them.

96
00:04:58,360 --> 00:04:59,620
You don't understand.

97
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:02,520
It's going to rain.

98
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:04,160
Yeah.

99
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:05,960
You predicted it perfectly.

100
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:09,480
Then why are you still standing here? Let's go.

101
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:11,720
If you let me get caught in the rain, you're dead.

102
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:13,120
I'll take you somewhere.

103
00:05:13,160 --> 00:05:13,840
Let's go.

104
00:05:21,440 --> 00:05:22,200
Shi'an,

105
00:05:22,200 --> 00:05:23,960
let's find a place to take shelter from the rain.

106
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:25,090
We're almost there.

107
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:48,520
Your wine.

108
00:05:49,960 --> 00:05:50,920
What is this?

109
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:53,520
This wine is really good.

110
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:55,600
How good? Is it expensive?

111
00:05:55,720 --> 00:05:56,800
As long as you don't bite me,

112
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:59,040
you can drink as much wine here as you want.

113
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:01,040
I have a high tolerance for alcohol.

114
00:06:01,520 --> 00:06:02,800
This bottle of yours

115
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:04,840
definitely won't be enough for me.

116
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:05,920
That impressive?

117
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:06,680
Of course.

118
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:08,120
Come on.

119
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:14,280
Miss.

120
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:15,280
What's wrong?

121
00:06:16,760 --> 00:06:17,960
I've dropped you off.

122
00:06:18,120 --> 00:06:19,120
I'll be going now.

123
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:20,200
Wait a minute.

124
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:22,240
You're completely soaked.

125
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:23,720
I'm afraid you'll catch a cold.

126
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:24,920
Dry yourself off over there first.

127
00:06:24,920 --> 00:06:26,780
I'll go find you some dry clothes.

128
00:06:27,800 --> 00:06:28,560
Alright.

129
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:30,960
Thank you for bringing me back.

130
00:06:31,960 --> 00:06:32,760
No problem.

131
00:06:39,560 --> 00:06:42,360
I told you I have a high tolerance.

132
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:46,800
Who just said they had a high tolerance?

133
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:47,480
Me.

134
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:49,000
I said it.

135
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:50,880
I have a high tolerance.

136
00:07:22,040 --> 00:07:24,040
Why aren't you wearing any clothes?

137
00:07:24,640 --> 00:07:27,100
How can I get dressed if you don't give me any?

138
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:29,680
Here.

139
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:36,120
Hurry up and put them on.

140
00:07:37,720 --> 00:07:39,120
Then leave.

141
00:08:01,320 --> 00:08:02,200
What's wrong?

142
00:08:03,160 --> 00:08:03,960
I'm fine.

143
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:05,960
Go back to sleep.

144
00:08:05,960 --> 00:08:07,820
Are you hiding something from me?

145
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:10,360
I want to tell you something.

146
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:45,960
Here.

147
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:50,360
Thank you.

148
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:52,720
Is the bread

149
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:53,960
good?

150
00:08:56,520 --> 00:08:58,380
Do you want to eat bread every day?

151
00:08:58,640 --> 00:08:59,440
Yes.

152
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:00,840
Come with me.

153
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:19,720
Does it hurt?

154
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:21,520
No.

155
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:24,640
Why did you risk your life

156
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:27,040
to save me today?

157
00:09:27,840 --> 00:09:29,440
You gave me bread

158
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:30,840
and took me in.

159
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:32,520
Of course I have to repay you.

160
00:09:46,040 --> 00:09:46,960
Father.

161
00:09:50,120 --> 00:09:51,520
His name is Wei Xiaodong.

162
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:16,600
Tonight,

163
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:18,880
at Shengfaxi Winery,

164
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:20,140
we are holding a party.

165
00:10:20,440 --> 00:10:22,440
Bring Wei Xiaodong over.

166
00:10:34,720 --> 00:10:36,360
Why have you never told me?

167
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:39,800
How could I say it?

168
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,640
It would cost lives if I did.
